                "retrieved_contexts": [
                  "October 2023 | ICC Policy Primer on Non-Personal Data | 18\nAbout the International Chamber of Commerce\nThe International Chamber of Commerce (ICC) is the institutional representative of more than\n45 million companies in over 170 countries. ICC\u2019s core mission is to make business work for everyone,\nevery day, everywhere. Through a unique mix of advocacy, solutions and standard setting,\nwe promote international trade, responsible business conduct and a global approach to regulation,\nin addition to providing market-leading dispute resolution services. Our members include many of\nthe world\u2019s leading companies, SMEs, business associations and local chambers of commerce.\n33-43 avenue du Pr\u00e9sident Wilson, 75116 Paris, France\nT +33 (0)1 49 53 28 28 E icc@iccwbo.org\nwww.iccwbo.org @iccwbo"
